III)\" across PDF 263-264; conclusion quote; glycolysis conflict cross-referenced correctly; baseline line 172. | (1) In When NOT add: \"Class 1 factor IV (2.7) is smaller than factor V (8.9), against the order of factors by share (verified against the page image); 2.7 may be a misprint (12.7 would restore the order and bring the column to about 98%), but the source gives no correction, so treat the 2.7 value as unclear.\" (2) In When to apply replace the Inference with: \"Inference: the rise of \"energetic efficiency of executing specific work\" to the first factor at Master of Sport level (36.5%) is consistent with that teaching point; the Class 1 value for the same factor (2.7) is unclear, so the size of the change should not be quoted.\" |\n\n## `_book.md` (4.3 and 4.4 rows, newest batch note)\n\n| Item | Verdict | Problem | Exact correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Rows 4.3 (241-247 / 252-258, done, 13) and 4.4 (248-254 / 259-265, done, 10) | GO | Entry counts match the scope list (13 files with chapter 4.3.x, 10 with 4.4). Page ranges match the source; the batch note explains that 4.3.6 runs onto PDF 259 and that PDF 265 / p.254 is blank (confirmed: text layer is only \"254\"). | None. |\n| Chapter 4 parent row (line 96: \"in progress \\| 6 (see section rows below)\") | FIX | The batch note says \"Chapter 4 is now complete; resume at Chapter 5\" and admits the parent row \"was not changed in this session.\" The map contradicts itself. | Set line 96 status to \"done\" and the count to the Chapter 4 total, and delete the sentence \"The Chapter 4 parent row still reads \"in progress \\| 6\" and was not changed in this session.\" from the batch note. |\n| Batch note content | GO | Section names, page spans, figure/table pages checked (PDF 253-257, 260-264), contested list and Pattengale note all match the entries. | None. |\n\n## Duplicates\n\nNone. The vault has Evans's applied wrestling case study (`elite-sports-performance--evans/case-study--dynamic-corresponden