ise-different-regime-boxer-vs-shot-putter.md","description":"Print boxer passage and read boxer entry"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffVHzt4PhykYcHJEnxd2","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"19aef6f2-b44a-4fe1-a502-1dcf2cd1976f","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:49:09.494Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"19aef6f2-b44a-4fe1-a502-1dcf2cd1976f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"2a81cff2-a7a8-4e62-bcc6-0c023068f2b2","agentId":"a3aafe568bae89c86","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YGNEdNvvKbC7ANrfCjADGP","type":"tool_result","content":"boxers and shot putters need to execute the same exercise  (e.g. performing a thrusting arm movement against the resistance of a pulley machine) with different weights,  tempos, number of sets and repetitions, because boxing requires primarily a quick, unresisted movement and the  ability to repeat it many times without significant decrease in force, whereas shotputting involves rapid single  movements against a specific resistance. The selection of a regime of muscular work is difficult where a specific motor action is concerned. However,  it is even more difficult in all-round sports like decathlon, gymnastics and modem pentathlon. Therefore, the  problem of selecting a regime of muscular work involves two obvious tasks: • selection of the regime for a specific motor action (e.g. the key elements in an exercise) • selection of the main regime which will best develop all of the diverse \n# The Same Exercise Serves Different Sports Only If Its Regime Changes: Load, Tempo, Sets and Repetitions Must Match the Sport's Work\n\n**What it is** — The fifth correspondence criterion \"relies on determining the character of the muscular work involved,\" and the regime \"should be taken into consideration for selecting the means and methods of special strength training,\" because \"depending upon the character of its execution, the same means can solve different tasks.\" The authors' example: \"boxers and shot putters need to execute the same exercise (e.g. performing a thrusting arm movement against the resistance of a pulley machine) with different weights, tempos, number of sets and repetitions, because boxing requires primarily a quick, unresisted movement and the ability to repeat it many times without significant decrease in force, whereas shotputting involves rapid single movements against a specific resistance.\" The problem has two tasks: \"selection of the regime for a specific motor action (e.g. the key elements in an exercise)\" and \"selection of the main regime which will best develop all of the diverse muscular activities in all-round training\"; the second \"is still far from being resolved.\" (PDF p. 258 / printed p. 247.)\n\n**Why it works** — The authors' reasoning is that the training effect is set by how an exercise is executed, not by the exercise's name or shape, so the regime parameters must reproduce the sport's demand (repeated fast unresisted actions for the boxer, single fast actions against a set resistance for the shot putter). They give no further mechanism.\n\n**When to apply** — After an exercise passes the movement criteria (amplitude, direction, accentuated region), set its loading parameters from the sport's regime: repeated low-resistance fast actions call for light loads, fast tempo and many repetitions; single maximal actions against a fixed implement call for heavier loads, few repetitions and full recovery. Eric's baseline: \"Exercise selection is organized on a spectrum from general preparation through specific preparation, specific development, to competitive exercises (Bondarchuk), replacing the loose and often-misapplied idea of 'sport specific.'\" Tagged **Inferred (transcript + slides)** (`docs/method-baseline.md`, line 102). Inference: this criterion adds that position on that spectrum depends on how an exercise is loaded, not only which exercise it is.\n\n**When NOT to apply** — The book gives the boxer and shot putter contrast without numbers, so it does not prescribe specific loads. For all-round sports (decathlon, gymnastics, modern pentathlon) the authors say the choice of a main regime is unresolved (see [[claim--all-round-athletes-main-regime-cyclic-and-phasic-tonic]]). Regime matching does not replace the other four criteria.\n\n**Example** — The book's own: a pulley-machine thrusting arm movement done by a boxer (light, fast, many repetitions) and by a shot putter (heavier, single fast efforts) (PDF p. 258 / printed p. 247).\n\n**Related** — [[framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence]], [[claim--regime-switching-ability-decides-mixed-regime-events]], [[claim--all-round-athletes-main-regime-cyclic-and-phasic-tonic]], [[framework--eight-types-of-muscular-tension]], [[heuristic--choice-of-muscle-training-regime-favor-combination]] (4.2, choice among isometric, eccentric and other regimes), [[elite-sports-performance--evans/case-study--dynamic-correspondence-applied-to-wrestling-takedown]] (Evans applies the regime criterion to a wrestling takedown).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ed6f7221-07cf-417e-859b-9d24a5589529","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:49:10.340Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"boxers and shot putters need to execute the same exercise  (e.g. performing a thrusting arm movement against the resistance of a pulley machine) with different weights,  tempos, number of sets and repetitions, because boxing requires primarily a quick, unresisted movement and the  ability to repeat it many times without significant decrease in force, whereas shotputting involves rapid single  movements against a specific resistance. The selection of a regime of muscular work is difficult where a specific motor action is concerned. However,  it is even more difficult in all-round sports like decathlon, gymnastics and modem pentathlon. Therefore, the  problem of selecting a regime of muscular work involves two obvious tasks: • selection of the regime for a specific motor action (e.g. the key elements in an exercise) • selection of the main regime which will best develop all of the diverse \n# The Same Exercise Serves Different Sports Only If Its Regime Changes: Load, Tempo, Sets and Repetitions Must Match the Sport's Work\n\n**What it is** — The fifth correspondence criterion \"relies on determining the character of the muscular work involved,\" and the regime \"should be taken into consideration for selecting the means and methods of special strength training,\" because \"depending upon the character of its execution, the same means can solve different tasks.\" The authors' example: \"boxers and shot putters need to execute the same exercise (e.g. performing a thrusting arm movement against the resistance of a pulley machine) with different weights, tempos, number of sets and repetitions, because boxing requires primarily a quick, unresisted movement and the ability to repeat it many times without significant decrease in force, whereas shotputting involves rapid single movements against a specific resistance.\" The problem has two tasks: \"selection of the regime for a specific motor action (e.g. the key elements in an exercise)\" and \"selection of the main regime which will best develop all of the diverse muscular activities in all-round training\"; the second \"is still far from being resolved.\" (PDF p. 258 / printed p. 247.)\n\n**Why it works** — The authors' reasoning is that the training effect is set by how an exercise is executed, not by the exercise's name or shape, so the regime parameters must reproduce the sport's demand (repeated fast unresisted actions for the boxer, single fast actions against a set resistance for the shot putter). They give no further mechanism.\n\n**When to apply** — After an exercise passes the movement criteria (amplitude, direction, accentuated region), set its loading parameters from the sport's regime: repeated low-resistance fast actions call for light loads, fast tempo and many repetitions; single maximal actions against a fixed implement call for heavier loads, few repetitions and full recovery. Eric's baseline: \"Exercise selection is organized on a spectrum from general preparation through specific preparation, specific development, to competitive exercises (Bondarchuk), replacing the loose and often-misapplied idea of 'sport specific.'\" Tagged **Inferred (transcript + slides)** (`docs/method-baseline.md`, line 102). Inference: this criterion adds that position on that spectrum depends on how an exercise is loaded, not only which exercise it is.\n\n**When NOT to apply** — The book gives the boxer and shot putter contrast without numbers, so it does not prescribe specific loads. For all-round sports (decathlon, gymnastics, modern pentathlon) the authors say the choice of a main regime is unresolved (see [[claim--all-round-athletes-main-regime-cyclic-and-phasic-tonic]]). Regime matching does not replace the other four criteria.\n\n**Example** — The book's own: a pulley-machine thrusting arm movement done by a boxer (light, fast, many repetitions) and by a shot putter (heavier, single fast efforts) (PDF p. 258 / printed p. 247).\n\n**Related** — [[framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence]], [[claim--regime-switching-ability-decides-mixed-regime-events]], [[claim--all-round-athletes-main-regime-cyclic-and-phasic-tonic]], [[framework--eight-types-of-muscular-tension]], [[heuristic--choice-of-muscle-training-regime-favor-combination]] (4.2, choice among isometric, eccentric and other regimes), [[elite-sports-performance--evans/case-study--dynamic-correspondence-applied-to-wrestling-takedown]] (Evans applies the regime criterion to a wrestling takedown).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"19aef6f2-b44a-4fe1-a502-1dcf2cd1976f","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
