{"parentUuid":"bb960966-5d92-43a2-ae62-e4e8a88a8abc","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3aafe568bae89c86","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffVWnazrgWXefQED2VJQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the five-criteria and accentuated-angle entries (Fig 4.22). I'll quote all three source sentences rather than the reviewer's one-sided framing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":849,"cache_read_input_tokens":120914,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":849,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffVWkAQ9w2jMjNTi4iTa","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0e8bb722-7217-483e-b511-42e83bba0437","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:51:56.950Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"0e8bb722-7217-483e-b511-42e83bba0437","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3aafe568bae89c86","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffVWnazrgWXefQED2VJQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L5d3dvJkZGKVPu8p67cEWs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence.md'; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\na=\"Inference: when the criteria conflict (for example, matching amplitude may require an awkward position that breaks the regime of work, as the authors' own Fig 4.22 discussion shows, PDF p. 256 / printed p. 245), the text gives no ranking among them.\"\nb=\"The text gives no ranking among the criteria. The authors say that following the amplitude and direction requirements \\\"can sometimes lead to such initial positions using weights or pulley machines which are incongruous and artificial (Fig 4.22),\\\" but that \\\"this occurs only when an exercise is attempted which fails to take into consideration the appropriate criteria,\\\" and they add that the Fig 4.22 exercise \\\"may be appropriate if applied carefully\\\" (PDF p. 256 / printed p. 245). So they do not treat the criteria as conflicting. Inference: in practice, meeting all five at once may still force a compromise; the book does not address that case.\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b); open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\n\np='heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle.md'; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\na=\"The authors also show a partner exercise (Fig 4.22, verified against the page image: one partner on the athlete's shoulders, another pulling the athlete's back leg, the athlete against wall bars) where trying to meet the criteria gives \\\"incongruous and artificial\\\" positions. Its caption\"\nb=\"The authors say that following these requirements \\\"can sometimes lead to such initial positions using weights or pulley machines which are incongruous and artificial (Fig 4.22),\\\" but add: \\\"However, this occurs only when an exercise is attempted which fails to take into consideration the appropriate criteria\\\" (PDF p. 256 / printed p. 245). Fig 4.22 (verified against the page image: one partner on the athlete's shoulders, another pulling the athlete's back leg, the athlete against wall bars) is a partner exercise in which, per the text, the partner on the shoulders \\\"simulates the vertical loading which sprinting normally imposes\\\" and the partner on the back leg offers resistance \\\"intended to strengthen the power of the hip flexors.\\\" Its caption\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b); open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"occurs only when\" framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence.md heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle.md | cut -c1-200","description":"Apply Fig 4.22 fixes to two entries"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":849,"cache_read_input_tokens":120914,"output_tokens":1126,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":25},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":849},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1126,"cache_read_input_tokens":120914,"cache_creation_input_tokens":849,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":849,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01L5d3dvJkZGKVPu8p67cEWs":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence.md'; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\na=\"Inference: when the criteria conflict (for example, matching amplitude may require an awkward position that breaks the regime of work, as the authors' own Fig 4.22 discussion shows, PDF p. 256 / printed p. 245), the text gives no ranking among them.\"\nb=\"The text gives no ranking among the criteria. The authors say that following the amplitude and direction requirements \\\"can sometimes lead to such initial positions using weights or pulley machines which are incongruous and artificial (Fig 4.22),\\\" but that \\\"this occurs only when an exercise is attempted which fails to take into consideration the appropriate criteria,\\\" and they add that the Fig 4.22 exercise \\\"may be appropriate if applied carefully\\\" (PDF p. 256 / printed p. 245). So they do not treat the criteria as conflicting. Inference: in practice, meeting all five at once may still force a compromise; the book does not address that case.\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b); open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\n\np='heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle.md'; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\na=\"The authors also show a partner exercise (Fig 4.22, verified against the page image: one partner on the athlete's shoulders, another pulling the athlete's back leg, the athlete against wall bars) where trying to meet the criteria gives \\\"incongruous and artificial\\\" positions. Its caption\"\nb=\"The authors say that following these requirements \\\"can sometimes lead to such initial positions using weights or pulley machines which are incongruous and artificial (Fig 4.22),\\\" but add: \\\"However, this occurs only when an exercise is attempted which fails to take into consideration the appropriate criteria\\\" (PDF p. 256 / printed p. 245). Fig 4.22 (verified against the page image: one partner on the athlete's shoulders, another pulling the athlete's back leg, the athlete against wall bars) is a partner exercise in which, per the text, the partner on the shoulders \\\"simulates the vertical loading which sprinting normally imposes\\\" and the partner on the back leg offers resistance \\\"intended to strengthen the power of the hip flexors.\\\" Its caption\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b); open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"occurs only when\" framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence.md heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle.md | cut -c1-200","description":"Apply Fig 4.22 fixes to two entries"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffVWkAQ9w2jMjNTi4iTa","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d021d0e9-9055-41f6-872d-d88308e70d9c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:52:03.538Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
