{"parentUuid":"350cdca8-75a1-476e-9e20-652447f7efaa","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3aafe568bae89c86","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffVqpdK9342M1UeTPfhB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":150995,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":893,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5672,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffVqn9yyYeCrLyiR7Z4r","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"35b015f1-096f-45c3-85d7-5b6d57d3fbcd","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:56:19.694Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"35b015f1-096f-45c3-85d7-5b6d57d3fbcd","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3aafe568bae89c86","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffVqpdK9342M1UeTPfhB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I applied all 8 entry fixes and the `_book.md` fix. I checked every one against the PDF page first, opening the page images for Fig 4.22 (PDF 256), the power equations (PDF 257) and Table 4.2 (PDF 264). Every claim in the review held up on the page. In four places I worded the fix differently from the review, and the log lists these under \"Disagreements with the review\".\n\n## Per-fix outcome\n| File | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `claim--power-equals-force-times-velocity-only-when-force-is-constant` | **Applied, with a change.** New title. `proven` now covers only the identity P = dW/dt = F·v, which holds at every instant for any force. The authors' constant-force condition is quoted with its page and called imprecise; my physics is labelled \"Inference:\". The error is multiplying an average or peak force by an average or peak velocity, and the entry ties that to the authors' \"It is inadequate to refer to average or peak force alone\". I rewrote the whole first sentence of Why it works, not just the clause the review deleted, because it still endorsed the constant-force claim as fact. I dropped the review's \"only\" from \"true only when one force value stands for the whole interval\", since average power also equals average force times velocity when velocity is constant. The slug is kept, so the RFD entry's link still works. |\n| `framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence` | **Applied, with a change.** The invented \"criteria conflict / regime of work\" line is gone. Instead of the review's paraphrase, the entry quotes all three PDF 256 sentences: the positions are \"incongruous and artificial\", this \"occurs only when\" the criteria are ignored, and the same Fig 4.22 exercise \"may be appropriate if applied carefully\". The page reads both ways, so the entry shows both. |\n| `heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle` | **Applied.** Added the missing \"However, this occurs only when...\" sentence, plus the text's own description of the two partners. |\n| `heuristic--parachute-resistance-sizing-progression-and-contrast-release` | **Applied.** \"Standard fluid mechanics\" is replaced by the authors' \"(actually the square of the velocity)\" with its page. I also quoted \"Naturally, running speed determines the degree of drag resistance\" so the size-and-speed point is in their words, and merged the two Inferences into one. |\n| `claim--parachute-resistance-tradeoffs-for-dynamic-correspondence` | **Applied.** \"Heavy athletes, athletes returning from lower-limb injury\" is now labelled Inference. |\n| `heuristic--same-exercise-different-regime-boxer-vs-shot-putter` | **Applied.** \"Full recovery\" is now labelled Inference. |\n| `case-study--high-jumper-factor-structure-by-qualification` | **Applied.** \"Less to plantarflexor power\" is replaced by a labelled Inference: the book reports a factor share, not a training cut. |\n| `case-study--skater-factor-structure-by-qualification` | **Applied, with one change.** The entry now flags that Class 1 factor IV (2.7) is smaller than factor V (8.9). The misprint guess is labelled Inference with its sum (35.9 + 23.3 + 16.8 + 12.7 + 8.9 = 97.6), and \"2.7% to 36.5%\" is no longer quoted. The table keeps the printed 2.7. |\n| `_book.md` | **Applied.** The Chapter 4 row now reads done, 64 (6 + 35 + 13 + 10, which matches the 64 Chapter 4 files on disk). The \"was not changed in this session\" sentence is deleted. |\n\n## New entry\nNone, and the scope file is unchanged. The OBLA idea is already covered: the endurance entry quotes \"Since OBLA depends on VO2 max...\" and the Christensen & Hogberg sentence, and the local-blood-flow entry quotes \"OBLA can rise\". The only sentence not captured is the opening \"Practical improvement of the metabolic processes...\" (PDF 260 / p.249). The log quotes it in full so it can go into the endurance entry later; that entry was not flagged, so I left it alone.\n\n## Grep proof\n```\nclaim--power-...:14:# The Authors Warn That P = F x V Is Misapplied\nclaim--power-...:16:Scope of `proven`: only the identity P = dW/dt = F·v, which holds instant by instant for any force (Inference, see Why it works)\nclaim--power-...:18:Inference: because dW = F·ds, the rate of work is dW/dt = F·ds/dt = F·v at every instant, whatever the force history, so the instantaneous product F(t)·v(t) is exact\nclaim--power-...:22:The authors' statement that P = F.V needs constant force is imprecise (see What it is)\ndeleted phrase count: 0 / 0      (\"gives a wrong instantaneous picture\" / \"The physics is sound\")\nframework--five-criteria-...:29:So they do not treat the criteria as conflicting. Inference: in practice, meeting all five at once may still force a compromise; the book does not address that case\nheuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle.md:18:but add: \"However, this occurs only when an exercise is attempted which fails to take into consideration the appropriate criteria\nheuristic--parachute-resistance-sizing-...:28:Inference: velocity-squared drag is the textbook drag equation, and this relation is the only part of the entry that could rate `proven`\nclaim--parachute-resistance-tradeoffs-...:25:(Inference: for example, heavy athletes or athletes returning from lower-limb injury; the book names no population)\nheuristic--same-exercise-...-boxer-vs-shot-putter.md:20:(Inference: with full recovery between efforts; the book does not state rest)\ncase-study--high-jumper-...:30:Inference: the falling plantarflexor share may justify a smaller plantarflexor emphasis, but the book reports a factor share, not a training reduction\ncase-study--skater-...:32:Class 1 factor IV (2.7) is smaller than factor V (8.9), against the order of factors by share (verified against the page image, PDF p\ncase-study--skater-...:30:so the size of the change should not be quoted\nold phrase counts: 0 (\"when the criteria conflict\", \"standard fluid mechanics\", \"2.7% to 36.5%\")\n_book.md:96:| 4 | The Means of Special Strength Training | 201-254 | 212-265 | done | 64 (see section rows below) |\nremoved sentence count: 0\n```\nAfter that grep I added one more label: the What it is sentence in the power entry now starts \"Inference: the authors' statement that P = F.V needs constant force is imprecise\".\n\nAcross all 23 scoped files: no body em dashes, no em dashes in titles, no review-history words, no wikilinks wrapped across lines, and 6 section headers in every file.\n\n## Lint\nThe original script is unchanged. My temp copy at `/tmp/flint_lint/lint_library_mac.py` swaps in the Mac vault path. It also needs the staging path pinned to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library`, because the script finds staging relative to its own location. Without that, a copy in `/tmp` reports 69 issues, almost all of them false \"unresolved link\" errors.\n```\nsupertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md: body em dash lines [12, 114, 115]\nTOTAL ISSUES: 1\n```\nThat one issue is the known false positive from the dashes in `_book.md`'s title and table, outside my edits. I re-ran the lint after the last edit and got the same output.\n\nThe power entry's file name still says \"only-when-force-is-constant\", which no longer matches its title. If it's renamed at promotion, the one link to it in the RFD entry needs updating. Nothing went into git or the vault.\n\nLog: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch4-3-4_applied.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":150995,"output_tokens":2724,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":20},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":893},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2724,"cache_read_input_tokens":150995,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":893,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffVqn9yyYeCrLyiR7Z4r","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ce2990e9-d953-443c-af4e-c24ab4a0e2cb","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:56:34.510Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
